1
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:10,330
(Passenger Drop-off Area)

2
00:00:36,310 --> 00:00:39,350
=Vow of Autumn=
=Episode 8=

3
00:00:48,079 --> 00:00:48,880
Sis?

4
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:49,960
What are you doing here?

5
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,000
I asked him over.

6
00:00:57,920 --> 00:00:59,259
The bulb in my kitchen burned out.

7
00:00:59,259 --> 00:01:00,280
I couldn't do it myself,

8
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:02,079
so I asked him to help.

9
00:01:04,219 --> 00:01:05,500
I brought a new bulb.

10
00:01:09,879 --> 00:01:12,239
You two are around each other a lot now.

11
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:13,739
Fine. Go change it.

12
00:01:13,739 --> 00:01:14,400
Get moving.

13
00:01:32,439 --> 00:01:34,579
You came this early to change a bulb?

14
00:01:34,579 --> 00:01:35,719
How helpful.

15
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:45,519
Oh,

16
00:01:46,099 --> 00:01:48,579
any single doctors at your hospital?

17
00:01:48,579 --> 00:01:49,359
Handsome ones?

18
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,480
Why don't you set me up?

19
00:01:51,799 --> 00:01:52,420
No.

20
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,519
How could there not be?

21
00:01:54,519 --> 00:01:55,760
It's a huge hospital.

22
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,319
I wouldn't introduce you anyway.

23
00:01:57,659 --> 00:01:59,140
You'd just torment my coworkers.

24
00:02:00,459 --> 00:02:01,359
Come on.

25
00:02:01,379 --> 00:02:02,719
We might hit it off.

26
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:05,879
Oh,

27
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,939
see those egg tarts on the table?

28
00:02:07,939 --> 00:02:09,360
They're from that shop I mentioned.

29
00:02:09,439 --> 00:02:10,599
Now I'm craving them.

30
00:02:10,599 --> 00:02:11,800
You never get me any.

31
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,520
I'll get you some next time.

32
00:02:16,759 --> 00:02:17,259
Good.

33
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,800
You said it.

34
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:19,520
Besides,

35
00:02:19,759 --> 00:02:21,680
don't forget to find me a cute guy.

36
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:24,099
Okay.

37
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:27,919
I'll go wash my hands.

38
00:02:52,319 --> 00:02:53,120
All done.

39
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:54,719
Thanks for your help.

40
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,699
Thank you.

41
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:03,520
Your nails look nice.

42
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:09,879
Just some polish.

43
00:03:10,919 --> 00:03:11,879
It suits you.

44
00:03:44,199 --> 00:03:44,719
Let's go.

45
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,599
Ms. Wen.

46
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,479
Your nails look lovely.

47
00:03:51,479 --> 00:03:52,080
New manicure?

48
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,159
Cut the sweet talk.

49
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:56,199
Get to work.

50
00:03:56,199 --> 00:03:57,000
We have a meeting.

51
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,960
Got your nails done

52
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,039
because someone liked them?

53
00:04:13,599 --> 00:04:14,259
Ms. Wen.

54
00:04:14,479 --> 00:04:16,439
There's something you should know.

55
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,360
You found out that my husband,

56
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:21,079
in order to hide marital assets,

57
00:04:21,480 --> 00:04:23,040
secretly pledged his company shares

58
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,420
to Dingsheng Capital

59
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:27,079
and funneled the money offshore.

60
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,000
Remember that?

61
00:04:28,959 --> 00:04:29,500
Yes.

62
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:31,180
Is something wrong?

63
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,319
My husband caught wind of it.

64
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,000
He's already

65
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,899
had the pledge on the shares

66
00:04:36,899 --> 00:04:37,480
released.

67
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:39,199
The money went back the way it came.

68
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,639
Now there's nothing left to find.

69
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:46,120
But I only got the statement last week.

70
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:47,439
It hasn't gone to court yet.

71
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,040
How did they find out?

72
00:04:49,699 --> 00:04:50,439
I don't know.

73
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:52,920
Anyway, that's how it is.

74
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,399
Aside from you and the client,

75
00:04:57,439 --> 00:04:58,360
who else knew about this?

76
00:05:00,579 --> 00:05:01,819
Just Chen and me.

77
00:05:02,139 --> 00:05:03,660
Then how did it get out?

78
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:09,800
Give me some time.

79
00:05:10,339 --> 00:05:11,839
I'll get to the bottom of it.

80
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,000
Two days.

81
00:05:13,439 --> 00:05:14,360
In two days,

82
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,579
I want an answer.

83
00:05:30,819 --> 00:05:32,139
As a surgeon,

84
00:05:32,139 --> 00:05:34,300
you must be used to the sight of blood.

85
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:36,399
Not really.

86
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,899
Sometimes,

87
00:05:37,939 --> 00:05:39,519
we get some unusual cases

88
00:05:39,519 --> 00:05:40,680
that are pretty interesting.

89
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,399
Like the other day,

90
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,720
a man was eating fish,

91
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,600
and a bone pierced his bowel.

92
00:05:46,959 --> 00:05:48,879
When he came into our ER,

93
00:05:49,019 --> 00:05:50,319
we removed

94
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,160
a 3-centimeter fish bone from him.

95
00:05:52,879 --> 00:05:55,319
Three centimeters? Through his bowel?

96
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,839
Wow, he must've...

97
00:05:59,240 --> 00:05:59,620
Cheers.

98
00:06:04,459 --> 00:06:05,240
You came

99
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:06,480
to the right person.

100
00:06:08,199 --> 00:06:09,000
What's wrong?

101
00:06:11,959 --> 00:06:12,500
Nothing.

102
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,040
Just someone I know.

103
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,319
What were we eating...?

104
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,040
Go on about that man.

105
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:19,699
Well,

106
00:06:20,079 --> 00:06:21,240
after we removed it,

107
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:23,040
he refused to leave.

108
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,360
He kept saying,

109
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,959
"What if there are lasting effects?"

110
00:06:25,959 --> 00:06:27,639
"I need a full checkup."

111
00:06:50,860 --> 00:06:52,079
The steak's really good tonight.

112
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,139
It is.

113
00:06:54,839 --> 00:06:56,019
Too bad

114
00:06:56,879 --> 00:06:57,879
someone spoiled it.

115
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:03,500
What a coincidence,

116
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,699
running into you here.

117
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:06,699
What?

118
00:07:07,199 --> 00:07:08,540
You own this place?

119
00:07:09,639 --> 00:07:11,000
I'm just curious.

120
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:14,600
That guy you're with...

121
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,040
Who is he?

122
00:07:31,439 --> 00:07:32,639
None of your business.

123
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,579
You're right.

124
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:38,519
I just think

125
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,259
you don't look like a match.

126
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:49,660
And that woman in white

127
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:50,800
is a good match?

128
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,040
We were just talking about work.

129
00:07:58,540 --> 00:07:59,100
And you?

130
00:07:59,459 --> 00:08:00,899
Work as well.

131
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:03,360
On making new friends.

132
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:35,010
(Passenger Drop-off Area)
